{
  "$comment": "Holdings deliberately RECLASSIFIED by the wallet-yield adapter family: the same token, the same amount, reported under a protocol identity instead of the generic wallet one. diff_snapshots.py uses this to downgrade the intended before/after churn to INFO, so a redeploy comparison shows the reclassification as expected rather than as ~120 lines of apparent breakage. It downgrades NOTHING on value OR on identity: a LOST/GAINED pair is collapsed only when the asset, the isDebt flag AND the exact amount all match, the LOST side is positionKind Wallet, and the GAINED side carries the positionKind AND the protocolBrand/protocolId/protocolSubId named here. Any pair failing one of those stays a DIFF.",
  "$identity_comment": "The three hashes per row are keccak256 of the kebab-case slugs in src/utils/ProtocolIds.sol, which is what a snapshot stores. They are declared because the migration's whole purpose is changing these fields: without them a Wallet row reappearing under the WRONG protocol's slugs (wstETH attributed to Sky, say) was accepted as RECLASSIFIED with no DIFF. Regenerate if a slug changes.",
  "$generated": "From script/config/nav-config/meta-balance-adapters/<chainId>.json; regenerate if that changes.",
